:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">If I am reinstructed, and you ask me to instr=
uct Brent then he will not charge you for carriage of the order (i.e. drafti=
ng it in liaison with the other side). That would be included within the bri=
ef fee. Obviously, if he has to go to court then he will charge for that (al=
ongside any other consultations that you require). The difficulty for him, I=
 envisage, is that because he does not act on a direct access basis, he woul=
d need to be instructed by me which would require you to instruct me. He cou=
ld not just otherwise draft the order because he would be without instructio=
ns from you. I say this because I want to make clear that neither he nor I a=
re attempting to charge you for something (i.e. the drafting of the order) w=
hich would otherwise have formed part of the brief fee on the basis of the o=
riginal instruction. I hope this is clear.<o:p></o:p></span></i></p><p class=
=3D"MsoNormal"><i><span style=3D"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,=
